* ======================================================================================
* SASSI-EDU tutorial example 8: embedded shear-wall building, subtraction methods against FV
* ======================================================================================
* What you learn
*   - how a reinforced-concrete nuclear-style building with a two-level basement is modelled for
*     SSI: SHELL walls and slabs with practice thicknesses, a 6.5 ft basemat, lumped equipment masses,
*     the excavated soil as SOLID elements (ETYPE 2) with the free-field layer properties, one
*     group and one L number per embedment layer;
*   - the manual's rule for the basement interior (manual 1.5.1 rule 11, EXCSTRCHK): the excavated
*     soil and the structure share only the nodes of the foundation-soil interface (the outer
*     walls and the basemat); the interior walls and the floor slabs inside the excavation have
*     nodes of their own at the same coordinates as the excavated-soil nodes;
*   - interaction-node sets generated with INTGEN on the same model: FV (all excavated nodes),
*     FI-FSIN (subtraction method, SM: lateral and bottom faces) and FI-EVBN (modified subtraction
*     method, MSM: FI-FSIN plus the top face at grade), with their counts (INTCOUNT);
*   - the comparison the manual asks for before a reduced method is used for production runs
*     (manual 1.5.1 item 6, ASCE 4-16 validation against FV): transfer functions, ISRS and wall
*     forces of SM and MSM against FV, at the basemat, the grade floor and the roof.
*
* Physics in one paragraph
*   ANALYS solves [(K_s - w2 M_s) - (K_e - w2 M_e) + X_ff] U = X_ff U'_f.  In FV every excavated
*   node carries the free-field impedance and load.  In FI-FSIN the 196 excavated nodes inside the
*   box and on its top face carry neither: the rows of these nodes keep only -(K_e - w2 M_e).  That
*   soil volume, held at the walls and the basemat and free at the top, has natural frequencies of
*   its own; near the first one the subtracted soil resonates and the SSI system gets a resonance
*   that does not exist (the "subtraction-method anomaly").  FI-EVBN holds the top face as well,
*   which raises those frequencies above the 20 Hz cut-off of this model.
*
* The building (80 ft x 80 ft, 26 ft embedded; x, y = -40 .. 40 ft): shear walls on x, y = -40, -20, 0,
* 20, 40 make sixteen rooms of 20 ft x 20 ft; the main block rises two storeys above grade and the four
* central rooms continue as a tower (x, y = -20 .. 20 ft) two storeys higher.  Section y = 0 (looking
* north):
*
*  z = 64              +-----+-----+         tower roof 1.5 ft, 90 kips
*                      |     |     |         tower walls 2 ft
*  z = 48              +-----+-----+         tower floor 1.5 ft, 130 kips
*                      |     |     |
*  z = 32        +-----+-----+-----+-----+   main roof 1.5 ft, 2 x 55 kips
*                |     |     |     |     |
*  z = 16        +-----+-----+-----+-----+   floor 1.5 ft, 2 x 175 kips
*                |     |     |     |     |   outer walls 2.5 ft, interior 2 ft
*  grade z = 0   +=====+=====+=====+=====+   grade slab 2.5 ft, 2 x 330 kips
*                #     |     |     |     #   # = outer basement walls 3.5 ft
*  z = -13       #-----+-----+-----+-----#   basement slab 2 ft, 2 x 220 kips
*                #     |     |     |     #
*  z = -26       #########################   basemat 6.5 ft
*               -40   -20    0    20    40    x (ft)
*
*   Concrete E = 576,000 ksf (4,000 ksi), nu = 0.2, 0.150 kcf, 4 % damping (ASCE 4 response level 1:
*   uncracked stiffness and 4 % damping, as the manual quotes it in its Damping Cutoff note).  The
*   slabs and roofs carry another 0.025 kcf for distributed equipment, piping and live load (about
*   38 psf on 1.5 ft).  A stair opening (10 ft x 10 ft) passes the basement slab, the grade slab and
*   the first floor.
*
* Site: 26 ft of medium-dense sand and gravel (Vs 1,000 ft/s, the embedment), 42 ft of dense gravel
*   (Vs 1,500 ft/s) and 39 ft of very dense gravel (Vs 2,100 ft/s) on rock (Vs 5,000 ft/s).  Mesh:
*   10 ft in plan and 6.5 ft vertically below grade: Vs/(5h) = 1000/(5 x 10) = 20 Hz = the cut-off
*   (the lambda/5 rule; the horizontal size is about 1.5 times the vertical one).  41 SSI
*   frequencies, 0.1 to 20 Hz.  Input: vertically incident SV wave, control motion in X at the free
*   surface, the RG 1.60 record of examples/data (PGA 0.324 g).
*
* What to observe (examples/README.md, Example 8; lesson 11 of the guided course):
*   - CHECK: no error and no warning for FV; FI-FSIN and FI-EVBN only EDU-12 (validate against FV).
*   - INTCOUNT: FV 405 interaction nodes, FI-FSIN 209, FI-EVBN 258.  On a model this small the 3930
*     equations of the structure and the excavation cost as much as the dense impedance: FV takes
*     only about 1.25 times as long as FI-FSIN in ANALYS.
*   - every transfer function is 1.000 at 0.1 Hz (within 0.02 %);
*   - FV: the tower roof X transfer function peaks at 2.78 at 6.5 Hz (fixed base, basemat clamped:
*     12.6 Hz); 5 % ISRS zero-period accelerations 0.28 g (basemat), 0.32 g (grade), 0.45 g (tower
*     roof) for a 0.324 g control motion;
*   - FI-FSIN follows FV within 2.2 % below 10 Hz, then resonates near 16 Hz where nothing should:
*     basemat X 0.92 against 0.29 and tower roof X 1.81 against 0.57 at 16 Hz, the soil enclosed by
*     the walls 18.4 against 1.8; the 5 % ISRS are up to 16 % too high at 15.1-15.9 Hz, the
*     basement-wall forces within about 1.5 %;
*   - FI-EVBN follows FV within 5.1 % (transfer functions; the vertical motion of the grade slab under
*     a 330-kip item at 20 Hz, X within 1.1 %), 1.2 % (ISRS) and 1.3 % (wall forces).
*
* How to run (the working directory must be the examples directory, see examples/README.md):
*     cd examples
*     ../.venv/bin/sassi run ex08_embedded_building.pre
*   or from the repository root:  .venv/bin/sassi --cwd examples run ex08_embedded_building.pre
* Run time about 1 to 1.5 minutes (three ANALYS runs of 41 frequencies); about 60 MB in examples/ex08*.
* Results: examples/ex08/ (FV), examples/ex08_fsin/ (FI-FSIN, SM), examples/ex08_evbn/ (FI-EVBN, MSM).
*
* Units: ft, kip, s.  Gravity 32.2 ft/s2.  Equipment given as weights in kips (MUNITS 1).
* ======================================================================================
MDL,ex08,ex08
TIT,Ex08 - embedded shear-wall building 80 x 80 ft, FV interaction set
GRAVITY,32.2
*
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------- soil profile
* L,<nm>,<thick>,<weight>,<Vp>,<Vs>,<pdamp>,<sdamp>   (ft, kcf, ft/s)
*   L 1-4: the four 6.5 ft EMBEDMENT layers (0 to 26 ft), one L number each (manual rule: an L
*          number may be repeated in TOPL for identical layers, but not for embedment layers); the
*          excavated soil of layer k uses L k (MACT below).  Strain-compatible properties.
*   L 5:   dense gravel, 26-68 ft, in 3.5 ft sublayers (Vs/(5h) = 86 Hz)
*   L 6:   very dense gravel, 68-107 ft, in 6.5 ft sublayers (65 Hz)
*   L 7:   rock half-space
L,1,6.5,0.120,2000,1000,0.04,0.04
L,2,6.5,0.120,2000,1000,0.04,0.04
L,3,6.5,0.120,2000,1000,0.04,0.04
L,4,6.5,0.120,2000,1000,0.04,0.04
L,5,3.5,0.125,3000,1500,0.03,0.03
L,6,6.5,0.130,4200,2100,0.02,0.02
L,7,3.5,0.145,10000,5000,0.01,0.01
