*
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------- numbering clean-up
* RMVUNUSED deletes the 32 separate nodes no element uses (room-centre positions of z = -19.5 and
* -6.5, between the interior walls); NCOM then closes the gaps (CHECK warns about every missing
* number).  Nodes 1-567 keep their numbers; the tower nodes become 568-617 and the separate nodes
* 618-781:
*     tower (i, j = 2..6):   z = 48: node = 568 + 5 (j - 2) + (i - 2);   z = 64: node = 593 + 5 (j - 2) + (i - 2)
*     basement interior (i, j = 1..7):   z = -13: node = 643 + 7 j + i;   z = 0: node = 725 + 7 j + i
*     (z = -19.5: 618-650 and z = -6.5: 700-732, the nodes of the interior walls)
RMVUNUSED
NCOM
*
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------- drilling rotations
* A flat shell has no stiffness about its normal.  FIXROT fixes that rotation at the nodes connected
* to shells alone (the superstructure and the separate basement nodes) and the rotations of the nodes
* connected to solids alone.  It does not act on nodes shared by shells and excavated solids: at the
* face-interior nodes of the basemat (normal Z) and of the outer basement walls at z = -19.5 and -6.5
* (normal Y or X) that no interior wall or slab meets, the rotation about the normal is fixed with D,
* row by row (first node, last node and increment 2 or 18 of each row).
FIXROT
VAR,BS,11,29,47,65
VAR,BE,17,35,53,71
FOREACH,BS,D,@BS[#],@BE[#],2,1,ROTZ
VAR,YS,83,245,155,317
VAR,YE,89,251,161,323
FOREACH,YS,D,@YS[#],@YE[#],2,1,ROTY
VAR,XS,91,253,99,261
VAR,XE,145,307,153,315
FOREACH,XS,D,@XS[#],@XE[#],18,1,ROTX
